body:
> So the third int should go through `XR_VERSION_PATCH` (which doesn't seem to do anything relevant but I'm no Khronos dev :P), but most importantly I think the first two can only be `1.0` or `1.1`, at least until we upgrade to some OpenXR 1.2.x SDK.

I don't think we need to use `XR_VERSION_PATCH()` in composing the version - that just extracts the `54` part of the full version integer in `XR_CURRENT_API_VERSION` by masking out the major and minor components.

If we wanted to do some more validation, though, we could validate that each part is greater than `0` but less than each component of `XR_CURRENT_API_VERSION`? So, something like (untested):

```c++
ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(int[0] < 0 || int[0] > XR_VERSION_MAJOR(XR_CURRENT_API_VERSION), false, "Invalid OpenXR major version");
ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(int[1] < 0 || int[1] > XR_VERSION_MINOR(XR_CURRENT_API_VERSION), false, "Invalid OpenXR minor version");
ERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(int[2] < 0 || int[2] > XR_VERSION_PATCH(XR_CURRENT_API_VERSION), false, "Invalid OpenXR patch version");
```

